From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:32:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 094/112] Filters: the per-sample ramp steps without a 64-bit
 division per coefficient

Filter::rampStep() divided each coefficient's change by the block's length in 64 bits (__udivmoddi4: the Cortex-A9 has
no divide instruction), ten times per filter per block: 47,000 instructions per 128 samples in the full test song
(4 % CPU). Now 1 / n once per set (a 32-bit division) and a multiplication per coefficient; the last sample lands
within 2n LSB short of the target as before within n. And rampPieces() leaves out its two logs where the cutoff moved
by less than a third of an octave (the usual case).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter.h   | 22 +++++++++++++++++-----
 src/deluge/dsp/filter/hpladder.h | 15 ++++++++-------
 src/deluge/dsp/filter/lpladder.h | 19 ++++++++++---------
 src/deluge/dsp/filter/svf.h      | 13 +++++++------
 4 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter.h b/src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter.h
index 46237a77..485010cc 100644
--- a/src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter.h
+++ b/src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter.h
@@ -151,10 +151,19 @@ protected:
 	// change renders exactly as before. haveLast_: whether there is a last block's configuration to move from
 	bool haveLast_ = false;
 	// Per-sample steps from `from` to `to` over n samples: sample k (from 1) takes from + k * step, the last one to
-	// within n LSB of `to` (under 2^-24 of the unit for a block of 128), and the next block starts from `to` exactly.
-	// Every change moves, however small: no threshold, no staircase
-	[[gnu::always_inline]] static inline q31_t rampStep(q31_t from, q31_t to, int32_t n) {
-		return (q31_t)(((int64_t)to - (int64_t)from) / n);
+	// within 2n LSB of `to` (under 2^-23 of the unit for a block of 128; short of it, never beyond), and the next block
+	// starts from `to` exactly. Every change moves, however small: no threshold, no staircase. The division by n is
+	// a multiplication by 1 / n, taken once for all of a set's coefficients (RampDivisor): the Cortex-A9 has no divide
+	// instruction, and a 64-bit division per coefficient per block was 4 % of the CPU in the full song
+	struct RampDivisor {
+		uint32_t inv; // floor((2^32 - 1) / n)
+		explicit RampDivisor(int32_t n) : inv(0xFFFFFFFFu / (uint32_t)std::max(n, (int32_t)1)) {}
+	};
+	[[gnu::always_inline]] static inline q31_t rampStep(q31_t from, q31_t to, const RampDivisor& div) {
+		int64_t d = (int64_t)to - (int64_t)from;
+		uint64_t magnitude = (uint64_t)(d < 0 ? -d : d) * div.inv; // < 2^64
+		q31_t step = (q31_t)(magnitude >> 32);
+		return d < 0 ? -step : step;
 	}
 
 	// A filter's coefficients are nonlinear in its cutoff and resonance (the ladders' feedbacks go with moveability^1..3
@@ -183,7 +192,10 @@ public:
 	// How many pieces a ramp from lastParams_ to params_ over n samples takes (1 to min(kMaxPieces, n))
 	[[nodiscard]] int32_t rampPieces(int32_t n) const {
 		int64_t pieces = 1;
-		if (params_.frequency > 0 && lastParams_.frequency > 0) {
+		const int64_t lo = std::min(params_.frequency, lastParams_.frequency);
+		const int64_t hi = std::max(params_.frequency, lastParams_.frequency);
+		// (Within a third of an octave, 2^(1/3) < 1.26, one piece: without the logs, the usual case)
+		if (lo > 0 && hi * 100 > lo * 126) {
 			// quickLog: 2^25 per octave
 			constexpr int64_t kThirdOctave = (1 << 25) / 3;
 			int64_t logs = std::abs((int64_t)quickLog(params_.frequency) - (int64_t)quickLog(lastParams_.frequency));
